In the PUT_LastIndexOfContract method, we add an assert statement that checks if the old list size was not -1 (i.e., if the list was not empty). If it was -1 (which would imply an empty list), then LastIndexOf should not return -1 either. Because -1 indicates that x was not found in the list, if the list is empty, LastIndexOf should return any valid index value (not necessarily -1). Therefore, our assertion is checking if the old list size was correctly not equal to -1, which is the expected behavior based on the definition of LastIndexOf method.--------------------Here are the output of the assert statements corresponding to the comments starting with "@@@" in the csharp code.

